Listing 2: Example of a data consumer

Reactive extensions provided by UniRx integrate seamlessly with FunnyZoo’s UI system. By placing subscription calls inside the `RegisterEvent` method, the subscription lifecycle is automatically managed. Data consumers should only consume resources when active, rather than listening continuously. 

Beyond convenient lifecycle management, Observables offer more than just an alternative approach to event handling. Their true power lies in the "reactive extensions"—operators that enable transforming, combining, manipulating, and working with sequences of items emitted by Observables. These operators allow composing asynchronous sequences declaratively, providing all the efficiency benefits of callbacks without the drawbacks of nested callback handlers typically associated with asynchronous systems.

For example, a smooth update animation can be applied to the money label by using a custom operator on the `MoneyObservable` before subscribing. In another case, the buy button linked to a purchasable item is conditionally enabled depending on whether the player has enough money. The same `MoneyObservable` can be transformed into a "has enough money" stream using the `Select` operator and then bound to the button’s enabled state. The final result is shown in Figure 5.4.
